uthor_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Found in the review of PR #149 (R449-1 S1, with the measurement in that PR's #17 table): a module-scope `$error` guard does not stop sv2v + Yosys elaboration. Yosys elaborates through it. Only `$fatal` stops it, and Verilator reports all three as warnings unless `-Wfatal`.\n\n**Guards that use `$error` today** (lines at PR #149's head):\n- `KL_pp_nvm_port.sv:188` (`g_tmo_check`);\n- `KL_pp_originator.sv:148`;\n- `KL_pp_release_merge.sv:37`;\n- `KL_srp_encoder.sv:147`;\n- `KL_acmp_nvm_shadow.sv:537`, `:544`;\n- `protocol_processor_top.sv:842-873`.\n\n**Acceptance:**\n- Every elaboration-time parameter guard in `hdl/` stops elaboration in every front end the project uses: Verilator lint, sv2v + Yosys, and xvlog/Vivado. Whether that takes `$fatal` everywhere or a per-front-end measurement is the lane's design decision, recorded in the coding rules.\n- A bench grades each guard's severity, not only its message, and a `$error`/`$warning` mutant is killed.\n- No guard changes its condition.\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/151/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/151/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}